{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound","id":1456379,"title":"Can Wights be blood-bound?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-08T17:38:08-07:00","id":1456379,"title":"Can Wights be blood-bound?","content":"Exactly what it says on the tin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T18:03:23-07:00","id":1456381,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine so. You would have to be careful though, but after that they'd be like a vicious dog that is fond of one person. Bonus points if they're a gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T20:17:46-07:00","id":1456387,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's like taming a wild animal with rabies. Great idea if you're insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T20:34:52-07:00","id":1456389,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a Nossie and a Devil Tiger walking their respective leashed Wights and Chih-Mei through the park late at night and exchanging training tips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T23:11:42-07:00","id":1456392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456389#post1456389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm imagining a Nossie and a Devil Tiger walking their respective leashed Wights and Chih-Mei through the park late at night and exchanging training tips.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of Aliens: Music of the Spears, where handlers walk an alien down the street on a leash and a mad musician wants to make a 'Symphony of Hate' from the aliens' screams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T00:14:25-07:00","id":1456393,"title":"","content":"Some wonderful inspiration for Vicissitude here. I envision a whole line of vicious pets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T03:02:17-07:00","id":1456399,"title":"","content":"They even form packs in the wild, and they retain their natures. Blood bond a pack of caretaker wights, they will be totally devoted to looking after you in the most horrifying and abusive ways possible!<br /> <br /> I imagine it's a lot like having a pet cat or dog. Since, according to the wiki, they keep their language merits, you know the bastards understand what you're saying they're just choosing to ignore you.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a more intelligent wight might try to blood bond you back...<br /> <br /> Actually since it seems kind of like wights retain their sapience, but disregard it, I wonder if you could use the blood bond to force them to re-engage... If the hungry dead can get a chih-mei onto a dharma, can a cainite get a wight onto a path?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-09-2021, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T03:25:02-07:00","id":1456402,"title":"","content":"In theory yes, in practice the damned thing is too visciously destructive to do much with. I tried it in game once all I got was a rabid dog which wouldnt explicitly attack me but had to be chained down at all times. Same thing for vaulderie. Velya the vivasectionist has one and all the little horror does is constantly frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T03:44:07-07:00","id":1456403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456399#post1456399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They even form packs in the wild, and they retain their natures. Blood bond a pack of caretaker wights, they will be totally devoted to looking after you in the most horrifying and abusive ways possible!<br /> <br /> I imagine it's a lot like having a pet cat or dog. Since, according to the wiki, they keep their language merits, you know the bastards understand what you're saying they're just choosing to ignore you.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a more intelligent wight might try to blood bond you back...<br /> <br /> Actually since it seems kind of like wights retain their sapience, but disregard it, I wonder if you could use the blood bond to force them to re-engage... If the hungry dead can get a chih-mei onto a dharma, can a cainite get a wight onto a path?</div> </div> </div> </div>For that matter, couldn\u2019t a Cainite Blood Bond a wight and use the Bond to guide the wight back to Humanity (kind of like re-domesticating an animal that\u2019s run away and gone feral)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T04:20:51-07:00","id":1456409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456403#post1456403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For that matter, couldn\u2019t a Cainite Blood Bond a wight and use the Bond to guide the wight back to Humanity (kind of like re-domesticating an animal that\u2019s run away and gone feral)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine so, but I also imagine that'd be a <i>lot</i> harder. The Paths of Enlightenment don't require the wight to learn to think and feel like their former human selves again, it needs to care enough to engage in thoughts other than feed/sleep/stay safe and build itself up from there but it doesn't need to change too much from what it is yet.<br /> <br /> Humanity needs it to reforge the instincts of a species that is, at this point, alien to it. I imagine an ex-wight on humanity would also be traumatised as hell, making humanity an even less stable path to walk.<br /> <br /> Although that might depend on the wight. A caretaker wight will have an easier time being dragged back into humanity while a bon vivant is a natural fit for the Path of Cathari. A director or autocrat for Inner Voice/Power...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-09-2021, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T05:38:00-07:00","id":1456417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456403#post1456403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For that matter, couldn\u2019t a Cainite Blood Bond a wight and use the Bond to guide the wight back to Humanity (kind of like re-domesticating an animal that\u2019s run away and gone feral)?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was something somewhere in I think BJD where it was said that Ashur wasn\u2019t a singular Antediluvian, but a term for when one of them became a Wight, with the further intimation that, at least for Antediluvians, this state was temporary and they eventually recovered their identities.<br /> <br /> I also believe one of the options for the sarcophagus at the end of BJD was that it contained one of the 2nd Generation who had been a wight but had essentially \u201cgone sane\u201d during his torpor and was now running on Humanity (and also that the 1-3rd Gens aren\u2019t nearly as strong as they pretend to be* and a good chunk of the Jyhad is just trying to cover that up using the fog of war).<br /> <br /> * in my home game I\u2019ve used this to say that Gen 1-3 have the same traits as a Gen 4 (but a lot more xp) because that\u2019s the plateau for the blood thickening and in a few centuries all the generations will have notably thicker blood (i.e. by AD 2200 the 13th Gen will have a blood pool of 11, 8th Gens will be able to learn the 6th dot of disciplines and 5th Gens will be indistinguishable from Gens 1-4 except for XP totals... also 17th Gens will be the limits of generations while 15th Gens aren\u2019t automatically Caitiff or thinblooded either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T06:15:00-07:00","id":1456421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456409#post1456409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine so, but I also imagine that'd be a <i>lot</i> harder. The Paths of Enlightenment don't require the wight to learn to think and feel like their former human selves again, it needs to care enough to engage in thoughts other than feed/sleep/stay safe and build itself up from there but it doesn't need to change too much from what it is yet.<br /> <br /> Humanity needs it to reforge the instincts of a species that is, at this point, alien to it. I imagine an ex-wight on humanity would also be traumatised as hell, making humanity an even less stable path to walk.<br /> <br /> Although that might depend on the wight. A caretaker wight will have an easier time being dragged back into humanity while a bon vivant is a natural fit for the Path of Cathari. A director or autocrat for Inner Voice/Power...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Very good point. I guess it would definitely depend on their Nature.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1328\" data-vbnamecard=\"1328\">Chris24601</a> thanks. I read BJD but I forgot the implications of the whole Ashur thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T08:29:03-07:00","id":1456435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456403#post1456403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For that matter, couldn\u2019t a Cainite Blood Bond a wight and use the Bond to guide the wight back to Humanity (kind of like re-domesticating an animal that\u2019s run away and gone feral)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. Once your Humanity, or Path, hits the round 0 they're gone forever. You can't really bring someone back from that without really powerful, and very likely mythical, magics or ritual.<br /> <br /> Even then the wight is very dangerous. Few wights can resist the call of a fear frenzy, and very few even try to resist frenzy at all. I said in a previous post that it's like dealing with a rabid animal, and this is why. One single frenzy stimuli is enough for the thing to turn on its master in a passionate rage or panicked fleeing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T10:44:05-07:00","id":1456440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456399#post1456399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They even form packs in the wild, and they retain their natures. Blood bond a pack of caretaker wights, they will be totally devoted to looking after you in the most horrifying and abusive ways possible!<br /> <br /> I imagine it's a lot like having a pet cat or dog. Since, according to the wiki, they keep their language merits, you know the bastards understand what you're saying they're just choosing to ignore you.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a more intelligent wight might try to blood bond you back...<br /> <br /> Actually since it seems kind of like wights retain their sapience, but disregard it, I wonder if you could use the blood bond to force them to re-engage... If the hungry dead can get a chih-mei onto a dharma, can a cainite get a wight onto a path?</div> </div> </div> </div>A while back, I actually had an idea for a custom Path called the Path of the Hound.<br /> <br /> It was inspired by Hellsing, which ran with the idea of vampires being slavishly loyal to masters (in the Manga and OVA, it was limited mostly to Alucard; in the TV series, it implied that more mortals held vampires in thrall that we don't see, including the final antagonist).<br /> <br /> The idea behind the Path of the Hound was that instead of using the vampire's own morality (for a certain value of morality) to keep the Beast at bay, the vampire offloaded moral responsibility for their actions onto a designated Master. The Master can be anyone - undead or mortal - that can maintain dominance over the vampire. To a certain extent, this dominance is willing on the part of the Hound, as they <i>want</i> someone to control them. By submitting their volition to the dictates of an owner, they abdicate responsibility for their Beast onto someone else. Though by that token, they require that the Master be strong enough to be worthy of service. Indeed, part of the dictates of the Path be for the vampire to encourage their Master to be stronger, including by &quot;testing the leash&quot; (i.e. forcing the Master to be mindful of their control and to reinforce it periodically, lest their Hound break free).<br /> <br /> <br /> While the Path of the Hound was designed predominantly for vampires who were not in Wassail - the iconic example would be one held by Blood Bond or by sorcerous control, defaulting to the Path to resolve the tension between their morality and the need to obey - I imagine it could work as a sort of jumping (back) on point for Wights under someone's control. In order to resolve the tension between the Beast's desires and their Master's dictates, the Wight adopts the Path. Possibly returning to their senses, though in the doubtless warped context of a devoted pet.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing would probably only happen after considerable time training the Wight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T12:09:27-07:00","id":1456447,"title":"","content":"The most accurate answer I think I can give on wights getting their sanity back is that there's no official system presented for it. <br /> <br /> The Path of the Hound mentioned above sounds like it could a good homebrew solution for a campaign where regaining sanity could be possible. A plausible explanation for why wassailing vampires are usually put down could be that self-serving vampires would more naturally respond to a socially accepted opportunity to kill an elder and free up its holdings for seizure by doing just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T13:18:10-07:00","id":1456452,"title":"","content":"In re a Wight &quot;reclaiming&quot; their sanity and returning to (any) Path:<br /> <br /> It <i>theoretically</i> could be done. However, the only vampires justifiably capable of it were given the &quot;penny-flavored Capri Sun&quot; treatment in the 1100's by the Tremere.<br /> <br /> In terms of <i>controlling</i> a Wight, it's another story entirely and one wouldn't actually need the blood bond to do it. If you're an elder with Animalism, you're in luck since certain elder-level powers are capable of controlling other vampires' Beasts. Which is the perfect segue into...<br /> <br /> In re Antediluvians and the Beast:<br /> <br /> Starting with Animalism 7, the vampire starts to gain specific control over their own Beasts, being able to enter and leave Frenzy at will. With Animalism 9, the methuselah basically gets the bonuses of Frenzy permanently without any of the drawbacks, chiefly preserving their higher function and morality. Those two powers predictably begin to blur the line between vampire and Beast, really raising the question of whether morality really applies to them in terms of actually falling to Wassail, and what the implications of that are.<br /> <br /> And Antediluvians get Animalism <i>ten</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T10:48:15-07:00","id":1456767,"title":"","content":"Antediluvians <b><i>can</i></b> get Animalism ten. I'd only bet on the Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Tzimisce antediluvians actually having developed the discipline that far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T09:13:22-07:00","id":1456812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456379-can-wights-be-blood-bound?p=1456767#post1456767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antediluvians <b><i>can</i></b> get Animalism ten. I'd only bet on the Gangrel, Nosferatu, and Tzimisce antediluvians actually having developed the discipline that far.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't specifically about Antes, to be honest. The example I like to bring up being baba haha, with her infamous humanity 0. A lot of folks like to write it off as early edition jank, and they have a point doing so. But, I think there's more to it, because of what animalistic 9 does...if a vampire with such power is under basically permanent controlled frenzy, what defines wassail is more or less moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T11:54:51-07:00","id":1456821,"title":"","content":"Using wights as shock troops is risky as hell - I'm reminded of Marauders using Bygones. Is dropping a Dragon on a Chantry or Lab effective? Yes. Yes it is. Surviving the consequences is the hard part.<br /> <br /> A blood bound wight on a figurative &quot;leash&quot; could be handy, but equating it to a pet dog might be a misstep. A dog has been bred for domesticity and submission over many, many generations. Instead picture a powerful roided out wolf on a leash, one who happens to like you a lot but is not even feral, let alone tame.<br /> <br /> That said, Dominate does work on frenzying vampires, so it would work on Wights. It's just +2 difficulty to activate, and failure could be more severe. Using Dominate 2, 3 and 4 to completely reshape a wight's &quot;mind&quot; and &quot;memories&quot; so that you're its &quot;father&quot; or &quot;mother&quot; could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T12:30:23-07:00","id":1456823,"title":"","content":"Way I see it, Dropping a Wight on someone works absolutely swimingly if nobody knows you have that wight (or nobody can recognize the wight) <br /> <br /> I'm a man of convention. Dogs, Machete gangs, gunmen, Dogs with bombs strapped to them. These things will solve your problems efficiently. But sometimes you want a mess. nothing would stir up the wonder of doubt more than dropping a wight on your opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T08:43:07-07:00","id":1456874,"title":"","content":"Wights seem usable, to a degree. If they're not hungry, afraid or angry then wights don't care about much. If it doesn't consider you a danger, and considers you more beneficial to it alive than dead, the wight is not inherently disposed to harm you... And as I type this I realise that, in other words, they're vampires. (disclaimer: wight passivity highly situational, safety not guaranteed)<br /> They're also capable of complex thought, as shown by their capacity to understand language. So it might be possible to make an &quot;agreement&quot; with a wight and get it to do things for you, possibly even follow complex commands. It will just go horribly, horribly wrong somewhere down the line.<br /> It might be possible, through time, to condition them towards manipulation and domination.<br /> <br /> A blood bond might make social rolls possible, and unless I'm imagining things, dominate is easier to use on a thrall anyway.<br /> Wonder if a dementation + blood bond combo would work. Use Eyes of Chaos to track down a wight with an appropriate nature (child, conformist, caretaker), blood bond it so that it &quot;cares&quot; about you which should hopefully make it more susceptible to social rolls, and then psychically drug it into mind-numbing apathy until such a time that you need to pull the trigger and detonate that bomb.<br /> <br /> More than attack dogs, it'd be an idea to domesticate them for research as they make fascinating areas of study.<br /> What happens when a wight commits diablerie on a vampire with a path rating? Does the victim become dominant, becoming the typical hybrid of diablerist and victim, with the victim's path rating? Effectively returning the wight to &quot;sanity&quot;? Or does the wight automatically win, gaining a whole new set of memories and knowledge it doesn't give a damn about (but may be able to exploit in some fashion)?<br /> <br /> As animalism affects the beast directly, can wights be communicated with using feral whispers?<br /> <br /> I'd love to get some kind of magical brain-scanner and observe their &quot;brain activity&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-15-2021, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}